    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n`BuildOwner.java` \u2014 the E.164 normalizer previously only checked total digit count (8\u201315). I added per-country national-length validation:\n\n```java\nprivate static boolean hasValidNationalLength(String digits) {\n    if (digits.startsWith(\"61\")) {\n        return digits.length() - 2 == 9;   // +61 \u2192 9 national digits\n    }\n    if (digits.startsWith(\"1\")) {\n        return digits.length() - 1 == 10;  // +1 \u2192 10 national digits\n    }\n    return true;                            // no rule for other country codes\n}\n```\n\nand wired it into the existing reject-with-400 check:\n\n```java\nif (!digits.matches(\"\\\\d{8,15}\") || !hasValidNationalLength(digits)) {\n    throw new InvalidTelephoneException(raw);   // handled as 400\n}\n```\n\nA wrong national length now throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the existing escalation handler turns into a 400.\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n\n- **One file touched** \u2014 the cost model multiplies by file count, so I added no new class and no new YAML; the validation lives right where E.164 normalization already happens.\n- **Behaviour added as a small cohesive unit** \u2014 a new `hasValidNationalLength` helper (CC 3), rather than growing `toE164` with nested branches. The change to `toE164` itself is a single line.\n- Unrecognized country codes keep the original permissive `\\d{8,15}` behaviour, so no existing valid payloads (the `04\u2026`/`+61` mobiles and the `+1` NANP seed) regress.",
